  "scope": "The product adapter owns the concrete EffectRequest, exact ContinuationImage specialization, released static ceilings and ordered consistency diagnostics. Existing VM imports are exact reexports; the generic explicit-policy request validator remains separate. The concrete deserializer still runs the closed current/legacy codec and full frame-before-correspondence admission. Its frozen codec oracle now invokes the independent frozen semantic validator rather than the moved implementation; 74 valid, 1332 malformed and 592 semantic cases retain wire bytes and exact errors. Existing 4200 frame/correspondence comparisons also pass. Direct adapter tests cover original field addresses, eleven overlapping refusal stages, preserved zero-output policy, mutable-data rechecks, lexical frame versus canonical request admission and explicit ingress bounds. A public memory test uses adapter requests through actual VM restore/resume: decoding changes neither VM; mutated budget refuses before admission; successful explicit restoration settles only the receiving VM. Product policy is not authentic capabilities, bounded ingress, canonical pending-source admission, a live clock, original-budget provenance or journal permission. Original VM restore revalidation, identity allocation, conflict checks, pending canonicality, leases and memory/SQLite transactions remain authoritative. No complete durable native VM, new native API, protocol schema change or completed extraction gate is claimed. Product version follows the unchanged Cargo manifest.",
